  "final_span": "200-day moving average line near $58. Momentum indicators in the short term are declining.\nReviewing the chart again reveals that the prices are creating what I refer to as an Arrow Chart Formation (indicated by the orange box above). It essentially forms a triple-top pattern, characterized by three consecutive peak penetrations that failed, and two additional failures, aligning with the price movement in the past several weeks.\nAlso see: Is a Triple Top Pattern Emerging on Stocks?\nThere are times when you want to \"add to a known profit,\" and then there are times when you want to \"fight the trend\" and buy at new highs contrary to what I three months ago. This situation is what I regard as a trap; while sales are significant, there is no justification for buying this stock at present.\nTake it easy for the next few weeks as prices may make a",
